{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QJacobiator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QJacobiator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.leibniz_coeff_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.leibniz_coeff_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L86-L105","doc":"The Leibniz coefficient `q⁻¹(1 - q⁻¹)` of the q-bracket vanishes\n**exactly** at the classical limit `q = 1`.\n\nThis is the coefficient-level counterpart of `jacobiator_classical`\nand `jacobiator_nonzero` above: those locate the vanishing of the\nJacobiator itself, this one locates the vanishing of the prefactor\nthat carries it, and shows `q = 1` is the only place it can vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.jacobiator_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.jacobiator_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L72-L84","doc":"The Jacobiator is non-zero for q ≠ 1 when the cyclic Levi-form sum is\nnon-degenerate (the fields are not all Reeb-invariant).  The `q ≠ 0`\nhypothesis of the field-based statement is no longer needed: `q` is a\nunit by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.jacobiator_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.jacobiator_classical","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L65-L70","doc":"The Jacobiator vanishes at q = 1 (classical Lie algebra). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.value","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L60-L63","doc":"The Jacobiator value:\n`Jac_q(U,V,W) = -q⁻¹(1-q⁻¹) · Σ_cyc dθ(V,W) · ℒ_ξ U`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.cyclicSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.cyclicSum","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L56-L58","doc":"The cyclic Levi-form sum `Σ_cyc dθ(V,W) · ℒ_ξ U` carried by the data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.lie_W","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.lie_W","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The Lie derivative ℒ_ξ W. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.lie_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.lie_V","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The Lie derivative ℒ_ξ V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.lie_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.lie_U","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The Lie derivative ℒ_ξ U. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.levi_form_UV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.levi_form_UV","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The Levi form value dθ(U,V). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.levi_form_WU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.levi_form_WU","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The Levi form value dθ(W,U). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.levi_form_VW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.levi_form_VW","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L44-L44","doc":"The Levi form value dθ(V,W). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.q","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The substrate parameter q, carried as a unit of `R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QJacobiator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QJacobiator","kind":"structure","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-jacobiator.lean#L35-L54","doc":"**q-Jacobiator data**: the geometric inputs to the failure of the\nJacobi identity for the q-deformed bracket — the substrate\nparameter `q` (a unit of the ground ring), the three cyclic\nLevi-form values `dθ(·,·)`, and the three Lie derivatives\n`ℒ_ξ(·)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}